  <div class="md"><h1>Apply the onprem split rules to shared infrastructure and re-measure AAI (covers open task #68)</h1>
<h1>Onprem allocation: applying split rules to shared infrastructure</h1>
<h2>Executive summary</h2>
<p>AAI on the onprem desk reads 62.1% against a 90% target [qid:07456c65], but the defect is not where the task card assumes. Tag coverage is 100.0% and the allocated pool (2,477.13 USD) is exactly the full 2026-07 Usage total [qid:f8b13338], so every usage row, including VMware Licensing, Colo Power &amp; Cooling and Storage Array, already carries a team. The entire unallocated remainder is the Purchase and Tax pool [qid:de117efd], which has no team dimension at all and therefore no split rule to fix. <strong>I cannot report a measured post-application AAI: it is not in the figures and producing it requires a re-run of the allocation engine on 2026-07, which is outside propose-only.</strong> The storage check for task #68 shows no growth step, which removes the measured trigger for request #5.</p>
<h2>1. Where the gap actually sits</h2>
<p>The allocation snapshot for 2026-07 [qid:07456c65] decomposes cleanly:</p>
<ul>
<li>Allocated (direct): 2,477.13 USD, identical to the 2026-07 Usage total [qid:f8b13338]. Usage is fully attributed.</li>
<li>Unallocated (shared/indirect): Purchase 1,400.00 and Tax 111.78 [qid:de117efd].</li>
</ul>
<p>Two consequences worth stating plainly:</p>
<p><strong>The three named shared assets are already split.</strong> VMware Licensing, Colo Power &amp; Cooling and Storage Array all appear as Usage services with per-service and per-team breakdowns [qid:9f2f688b, qid:5a353afd], inside the 100%-attributed pool. Rewriting their split rules moves money between <code>sre-platform</code>, <code>ml</code>, <code>product-web</code> and <code>data</code>; it does not move a single dollar from unallocated to allocated, so it cannot raise AAI. The task card's premise is not supported by the measurement.</p>
<p><strong>The real blocker is that Purchase has no asset breakdown.</strong> Purchase is 1,400.00 in both 2026-07 and 2026-08 [qid:5a353afd], a flat recurring pool. The figures do not say which assets it covers (array capex amortisation, licence subscription, colo contract, or a mix). Without that, no defensible driver can be attached to it. This is the one input that gates the whole exercise.</p>
<h2>2. Proposed split rules (propose-only, not applied)</h2>
